      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/devario-annandalei-2/",
      "html": "<p>Devario annandalei becomes about 10 cm long. It is a schooling fish whose caudal fin has conspicuous red skin between the rays, hence the common name \"blood tail\".</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/devario-annandalei-2/",
      "html": "<p>Devario annandalei originates from Burma (Myanmar) and from subtropical regions.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/devario-annandalei-2/",
      "html": "<p>In respect of keeping and breeding there are no essential differences to the very well known Devario malabaricus. The only exception is water temperature. As D. annandalei originates from subtropical regions, it is recommended to keep it a bit cooler (room temperature) at times.</p>"
    }
  ],
